# .gitignore — anvil-git-policy: v7 · generated and maintained by Anvil
# Decides which files under .anvil/ are versioned (policy explained below)
# To customize, delete the `anvil-git-policy: v<n>` marker line at the top of this
# file — Anvil will stop overwriting it (and stop upgrading its policy for you).

# -- Not versioned: machine-local derivatives ------------------------------
# Source index pack and its derivatives (purely local, rebuildable by scan)
agent/repomix.md
agent/repomix.index.json
agent/meta.json
agent/meta-inputs.md
agent/meta-inputs-manifest.json

# Freshness / sync snapshots (timestamped local cache)
# Note: .meta/* rather than .meta/, so human.json, confluence-sync.json, jira-sync.json,
# and repo-settings.json can be allow-listed below
.meta/*
!.meta/human.json

# Confluence sync mapping (doc -> page ID/version) -- shared on purpose: if two
# teammates each sync independently with no shared mapping, they'd each create a
# duplicate Confluence page for the same doc. Never contains the API token itself
# (that stays in each person's own OS keychain), only structural doc<->page links.
!.meta/confluence-sync.json

# Jira sync mapping (backlog item -> issue key) -- shared for the same reason: without
# it, two teammates pushing independently would each create a duplicate Jira issue for
# the same item. Never contains the API token itself.
!.meta/jira-sync.json

# Repo settings (e.g. the default branch feature/bug work is cut from and merged back
# into) -- a team convention, not a machine-local cache, so it travels with the repo.
!.meta/repo-settings.json

# Local environment state (tool paths, integration manifest)
env/

# Intermediate workspace for generation runs
.litho-agent/
.sdd-agent/
.agent-ctx-workspace/

# ARB review deck output (a build artifact regenerable via Create/Refresh, not a knowledge doc)
agent/arb-deck/

# OS noise
.DS_Store

# -- Versioned (not excluded by the rules above) ---------------------------
# knowledge/   hand-maintained private-domain knowledge -- the part that
#              genuinely needs line-by-line merging
# agent/context.md, human/, index.md, project-note.md
#              generated knowledge documents; merge strategy in .gitattributes
# agent/context-meta.json, .meta/human.json
#              provenance metadata for versioned documents (baseline git HEAD /
#              generation time). This must travel with the content it
#              describes -- otherwise another clone pairs fresh documents with
#              a stale local baseline and freshness scoring diverges across
#              machines, with no way to self-correct.
